@@ -3,8 +3,27 @@
 A tools-management panel plugin: the host half attributes every registered
 tool to its source plugin (collapsible prefix tree) and globally disables
 individual tools through a two-layer gate; the browser half registers the
-settings-page tools tab through the `settings.section` slot. Written in the
-0.1.0-era style; the host is moving to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+settings-page tools tab through the `settings.section` slot. Targets dsh
+0.1.2-alpha.2: the client half uses the split client plane (the loader bundle
+envelope, `ctx.slots` from `dsh-client-ui-renderer`, the `settings.section`
+key from `dsh-client-ui-settings`), and the host half resolves `webServer`
+optionally so a profile without a browser surface still activates the tool
+registry and the gate.
+
+Documented entry points:
+
+- `settings.section` settings tab (`id: bench-tools-tree`, order 62, label
+  工具管理), served by the package's `./client` export.
+- Tool-to-source-plugin attribution and the two-layer enable/disable gate
+  (`system-prompt/assemble` hides disabled tools; `ctx.tools.guard()` denies
+  execution).
+- `POST /tools-manager/api/list` and `POST /tools-manager/api/set` on the
+  `webServer` prefix route `/tools-manager/api`, registered only while a
+  browser surface is composed.
+- The `disabled` set persists through the plugin's own `tools-manager`
+  settings namespace (`ctx.settings.installSection`), applied without restart.
+- Distribution as a self-contained outer bundle: `dsh.bundle.patch` inserts
+  the host row, `dsh.client` declares the browser half.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
